window.STUDY={"id":"ap-17-lid-insert","code":"AP-17","title":"Lid insert · a hill in laser power","fig":"4.17","kicker":"Application · 17","lede":"The card insert for a tea tin, burned by a laser.","body":["The garden's hill is a contour map in which the beam's power is the elevation: one power step (7.5 %) for every 100 m above 600 m, so the bands darken as the hill rises, and the 1,000 m and 1,500 m index lines burn at full power. The legend is burned at the same steps. The summit figure is burned too; the rest is printed. A fictional hill."],"source":"Made with the effect set: Laser char, Roller run-out, Paper tooth.","ref":{"w":1500,"h":1875},"variants":[{"id":"set","label":"As drawn","sw":[]}],"points":[],"colorHint":"The inks are dials of the effects: open Parameters and pick an effect.","paramsHint":"Every dial of the effects this piece uses.","spec":{"usage":{"id":"u-contour","job":"packaging","title":"Lid insert · a hill in laser power","aspect":"4/5","uses":["fx-12-laser","fx-02-ink-edge","fx-03-paper-tooth"]},"reference":{"grammar":"The card insert for a tea tin, burned by a laser. The garden's hill is a contour map in which the beam's power is the elevation: one power step (7.5 %) for every 100 m above 600 m, so the bands darken as the hill rises, and the 1,000 m and 1,500 m index lines burn at full power. The legend is burned at the same steps. The summit figure is burned too; the rest is printed. A fictional hill."},"techniques":[{"id":"fx-12-laser","name":"Laser char","short":"FX-12","atoms":["burn"],"params":{"size":{"value":0.7,"range":[0.15,1],"label":"Size","step":0.01,"note":"motif height as a share of the plate"},"power":{"value":0.92,"range":[0.05,1],"label":"Power","step":0.01,"note":"beam power in the raster; dose ∝ power ÷ speed ÷ pitch"},"speed":{"value":1,"range":[0.25,3],"label":"Speed","step":0.01,"note":"head speed (relative); faster = less dose per line"},"pitch":{"value":1.5,"range":[1,6],"label":"Line pitch","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"distance between scan lines; clamped to ≥ 2 device px, with the dose scaled to match"},"scan":{"value":0,"range":[0,180],"label":"Scan angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"direction the head travels"},"spot":{"value":0.5,"range":[0.3,2],"label":"Spot","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"beam radius σ in focus"},"focus":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Defocus","step":0.01,"note":"0 = in focus; out of focus the spot widens and its peak drops"},"ramp":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Power ramp","step":0.01,"note":"power falls across the raster, to 15 % at 1"},"rampAng":{"value":0,"range":[0,360],"label":"Ramp angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"direction the power falls along"},"overburn":{"value":0.08,"range":[0,1],"label":"Turnaround burn","step":0.01,"note":"extra dose where the head slows to reverse at each line end"},"halo":{"value":0.3,"range":[0,1],"label":"Heat halo","step":0.01,"note":"fibers browned around the burn"},"haloR":{"value":1.4,"range":[0.5,12],"label":"Halo reach","step":0.1,"unit":"px","note":"how far the heat browns the fibers around the burn"},"ablate":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1.5],"label":"Ablation","step":0.01,"unit":"px","note":"how far the surface sinks at full char"},"diffuse":{"value":0.9,"range":[0,1],"label":"Diffuse share","step":0.01,"note":"share of light from the sheet light vs flat ambient fill"},"kerf":{"value":1.3,"range":[0.4,4],"label":"Kerf","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"width of the cut"},"cutOff":{"value":10,"range":[2,40],"label":"Cut offset","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"distance from the motif edge to the cut"},"tabs":{"value":4,"range":[0,8],"label":"Tabs","step":1,"note":"uncut bridges that hold the part"},"tabW":{"value":4,"range":[1,14],"label":"Tab width","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"width of each bridge"},"thick":{"value":1.4,"range":[0.2,4],"label":"Card thickness","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"sizes the card edge's shadow on the ground in the kerf"},"gL":{"value":0.17,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ground below · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"gC":{"value":0.006,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Ground below · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"gh":{"value":255,"range":[0,360],"label":"Ground below · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"seed":{"value":12,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Scan lines at the pitch (≥ 2 device px), at the scan angle. Dose at a pixel = Σ over nearby lines of power ÷ speed × the beam's gaussian, integrated over the pixel (erf): anti-aliased lines at any angle. When the pitch clamps to 2 device px, the dose is scaled by the clamp so the tone matches a finer screen. Firing gate = the motif clip sampled at each line's centerline, softened by the spot along the scan; the head's turnaround adds dose just inside the edges it reverses at. Defocus widens σ and lowers the peak (same energy, larger spot): paler, softer, lines merging. A power ramp can run across the raster. Char = 1 − e^(−k·(dose − threshold)) → an OKLab ramp tan → brown → black, multiplied into the stock albedo (fibers char darker). Heat halo = the dose spread a few px, browning fibers first. Relief: ablation sinks the surface with dose; the tooth is burned smooth; a fine char crust. Lit by the sheet light (grooves catch it on one wall). Vector cut: a kerf along the motif outline (offset) or a tag; tabs leave bridges. The kerf opens onto the ground below, shaded by the card edge toward the light; its walls are charred.","limits":"line pitch < 2 device px: clamped: finer lines alias into moiré on screen (dose is conserved). power ÷ speed > 1.4: char goes black and ablates; line structure survives only in the relief. defocus > .7: reads as a smudge, not a laser. halo reach > 9 px: reads as a scorch accident rather than a mark. kerf > 3 px: a slot, not a laser cut"},{"id":"fx-02-ink-edge","name":"Roller run-out","short":"FX-02","atoms":["deposit"],"params":{"streak":{"value":1.25,"range":[1,10],"label":"Streak","step":0.1,"note":"film-split clumps stretched along the stroke: a dry roller, a dragged brush"},"pressure":{"value":1,"range":[0.4,1],"label":"Roller pressure","step":0.01,"note":"pressure in the solid; below 1 the body starts to open up"},"angle":{"value":0,"range":[0,360],"label":"Stroke angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"direction the roller travels (it runs out along this vector)"},"edge":{"value":1.7,"range":[0,1.7],"label":"Edge position","step":0.005,"note":"where the run-out is centered across the plate"},"width":{"value":4,"range":[1,420],"label":"Transition","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"width of the run-out band"},"wAmp":{"value":18,"range":[0,90],"label":"Edge warp","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far the edge line wanders"},"wScale":{"value":90,"range":[8,400],"label":"Warp scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander"},"wOct":{"value":3,"range":[1,5],"label":"Warp octaves","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"detail in the wander"},"bite":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,1],"label":"Stock bite","step":0.01,"note":"how much the stock height (vs film-splitting noise) decides where ink lands"},"breakup":{"value":1,"range":[0,1],"label":"Break-up ↔ thin","step":0.01,"note":"1 = ink film breaks into marks on the peaks as pressure falls; 0 = the film stays whole and thins to tone"},"starve":{"value":0.004,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Starve","step":0.002,"note":"the lowest share of the surface never takes ink. Pinholes in the solid, placed by the paper's valleys and pits"},"wick":{"value":0.03,"range":[0,1],"label":"Wick","step":0.01,"note":"ink carried along fibers into the run-out (hairline feathering)"},"mottle":{"value":0.05,"range":[0,1],"label":"Mottle","step":0.01,"note":"paper formation (its low-frequency cloudiness) varying the film thickness"},"split":{"value":1.1,"range":[0.5,10],"label":"Film split","step":0.1,"unit":"px","note":"clump size of the film-splitting noise (the roller's own speckle)"},"iL":{"value":0.18,"range":[0,1],"label":"Ink · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"iC":{"value":0.005,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Ink · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"ih":{"value":280,"range":[0,360],"label":"Ink · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"density":{"value":1.3,"range":[0.2,2],"label":"Film thickness","step":0.01,"note":"ink film at full pressure (Beer–Lambert: thicker = deeper, more saturated)"},"mInset":{"value":14,"range":[0,120],"label":"Inset","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"distance from the plate edge to the mask edge"},"mAmp":{"value":5,"range":[0,40],"label":"Edge wander","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far noise pushes the edge in and out"},"mScale":{"value":60,"range":[4,240],"label":"Wander scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander; small = ragged, large = drifting"},"mRough":{"value":4,"range":[1,6],"label":"Roughness","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"octaves of edge noise: adds fine teeth without moving the large shape"},"mFeather":{"value":14,"range":[0.5,60],"label":"Feather","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"width over which coverage falls from 1 to 0"},"mBite":{"value":0.2,"range":[0,1],"label":"Bite","step":0.01,"note":"clumped dropouts that grow more likely toward the edge"},"seed":{"value":9,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Pressure = dropoff curve of the signed distance to a warped edge line (stroke direction, transition width), × the mask. Ink chain: the stock height under the inked area (blended with film-splitting noise, clumped and streaked along the stroke) is ranked to percentiles; pressure P inks exactly the top P of the surface, peaks first. Starve: valleys below the threshold never take ink. Wick: fibers carry ink past the edge. Mottle: paper formation thins the film. Film thickness thins with pressure unless the film breaks up; color = Beer–Lambert film in linear light. Light last: × the stock's shading. The ink sits in the tooth, not on top of it.","limits":"transition < 4 px: reads as a hard vector edge: no run-out to see. break-up < .3: the edge becomes a gradient: the \"AI gradient\" failure. stock bite < .3: speckle stops following the paper and reads as digital dither. streak > 6: marks read as scanlines unless the angle is off-axis"},{"id":"fx-03-paper-tooth","name":"Paper tooth","short":"FX-03","atoms":["form"],"params":{"scale":{"value":1.1,"range":[0.5,24],"label":"Tooth scale","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"feature size of the tooth (noise wavelength), not a tile zoom"},"oct":{"value":3,"range":[1,6],"label":"Octaves","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"layers of finer detail"},"fibers":{"value":2.2,"range":[0,40],"label":"Fibers","step":0.25,"unit":"/100×100 px","note":"laid fibers per 100 × 100 CSS px"},"fLen":{"value":14,"range":[2,80],"label":"Fiber length","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"mean fiber length"},"fWidth":{"value":0.4,"range":[0.2,3],"label":"Fiber width","step":0.02,"unit":"px","note":"mean fiber width"},"pits":{"value":0.3,"range":[0,40],"label":"Pits","step":0.25,"unit":"/100×100 px","note":"depressions per 100 × 100 CSS px"},"pers":{"value":0.42,"range":[0.15,0.85],"label":"Persistence","step":0.01,"note":"amplitude kept per octave: the spectral dropoff of the tooth"},"aniso":{"value":1.5,"range":[1,6],"label":"Anisotropy","step":0.05,"note":"tooth stretched along the grain angle. Machine-made paper is never isotropic; 1 = the 1999 \"paper\" filter look"},"form":{"value":0.1,"range":[0,1],"label":"Formation","step":0.01,"note":"low-frequency cloudiness of the sheet (fiber flocs); also mottles any ink printed on it"},"formScale":{"value":60,"range":[10,200],"label":"Formation scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"size of the flocs"},"fAngle":{"value":6,"range":[0,180],"label":"Grain angle","step":1,"unit":"°","note":"machine direction of the fibers and the tooth"},"fSpread":{"value":0.4,"range":[0,1],"label":"Grain spread","step":0.01,"note":"0 = all fibers on the grain; 1 = any direction"},"depth":{"value":0.02,"range":[0,1.6],"label":"Relief","step":0.005,"unit":"px","note":"height of the tooth in CSS px: how hard the light can rake it. The slider is weighted to the subtle end."},"diffuse":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Diffuse share","step":0.01,"note":"share of light from the sheet light vs flat ambient fill"},"fRaise":{"value":0.45,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fiber raise","step":0.01,"note":"how far fibers stand proud of the sheet"},"pDepth":{"value":0.35,"range":[0,1],"label":"Pit depth","step":0.01,"note":"how deep pits go"},"paperL":{"value":0.968,"range":[0.85,1],"label":"Paper L","step":0.001,"note":"OKLab lightness of the stock under the sheet light. Below 1 so lit walls, foil and sheen have headroom to brighten; 1 = the white of the page (highlights clip)"},"fDark":{"value":0.014,"range":[0,0.15],"label":"Fiber tone","step":0.001,"unit":"ΔL","note":"albedo darkening of fibers"},"pDark":{"value":0.02,"range":[0,0.3],"label":"Pit tone","step":0.001,"unit":"ΔL","note":"albedo darkening in pits"},"tL":{"value":0.7,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fill tint · L","step":0.005,"note":"OKLCH lightness (0 black … 1 white)"},"tC":{"value":0,"range":[0,0.37],"label":"Fill tint · C","step":0.002,"note":"OKLCH chroma; reduced at constant L/h if it leaves sRGB"},"th":{"value":250,"range":[0,360],"label":"Fill tint · h","step":0.5,"unit":"°","note":"OKLCH hue angle"},"tAmt":{"value":0.5,"range":[0,1],"label":"Fill tint amount","step":0.01,"note":"how much the ambient fill takes the tint (shadows go cool / warm)"},"mInset":{"value":22,"range":[0,120],"label":"Inset","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"distance from the plate edge to the mask edge"},"mAmp":{"value":2.5,"range":[0,40],"label":"Edge wander","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"how far noise pushes the edge in and out"},"mScale":{"value":28,"range":[4,240],"label":"Wander scale","step":1,"unit":"px","note":"wavelength of the wander; small = ragged, large = drifting"},"mRough":{"value":5,"range":[1,6],"label":"Roughness","step":1,"unit":"oct","note":"octaves of edge noise: adds fine teeth without moving the large shape"},"mFeather":{"value":1.2,"range":[0.5,60],"label":"Feather","step":0.5,"unit":"px","note":"width over which coverage falls from 1 to 0"},"lift":{"value":1,"range":[0,4],"label":"Sheet lift","step":0.05,"unit":"px","note":"thickness / curl of the sheet: sizes its shadow on the page"},"mBite":{"value":0,"range":[0,1],"label":"Bite","step":0.01,"note":"clumped dropouts that grow more likely toward the edge"},"seed":{"value":21,"range":[1,999],"label":"Seed","step":1,"note":"every random draw in the effect derives from this one number"}},"implementation":"Height = fbm at the tooth scale (octaves, persistence = how fast detail drops off), reshaped by the distribution curve; blended with low-frequency formation. Fibers: curved capsules at a count per 100 × 100 CSS px near the grain angle, raised into the height; pits: small depressions. Both also darken the albedo slightly. Normal from the height gradient → Lambert under the sheet light (azimuth + elevation from the light puck). Diffuse share vs ambient fill; the fill can be tinted. The same field is the stock for FX-01 and FX-02: its peaks take ink first, its valleys starve, its fibers wick. Mask = the sheet's cut or deckle edge; the sheet casts a contact + ambient shadow onto the page by the same light.","limits":"relief > .6 px: reads as stucco: the stock-filter emboss look. anisotropy < 1.3: isotropic tooth reads as a 1999 paper filter. tooth scale < .8 px: collapses into per-pixel noise: digital grain. fibers > 30 /100×100 px: felt, not paper. light elevation < 15°: every fiber becomes a hard ridge; ok for a raking-light study, not for a page"}],"pass_order":["Laser char · A CO₂ beam rasters a motif into card, one scan line at a time.","Roller run-out · A solid that runs out.","Paper tooth · White stock that is not a screen."]}};
